    "heading": "Name the decision and the queue owner",
    "body": "In the QBR action log workflow, a quarterly business review arrives before anyone confirms the client, the period, or the responsible queue. Every QBR action log case carries a stable reference before the action list or the owner is attached. A QBR action log case that crosses a shift keeps the original requester visible beside the new owner. The QBR action log queue shows the promised response time, the current owner, and the next action. Review pass 1.1: the account team files the QBR action log evidence.\n\nThe QBR action log working file joins the action list, the owner, the due date, and the client note on one case reference so the decision can be rebuilt. The QBR action log decision is written in one sentence so a second reviewer can tell whether the case is finished. For QBR action log, the queue entry names the client, the period, the requester, and the person who can close the question. Review pass 1.2: the account team files the QBR action log evidence."
